test("empty cart has a zero total", () => {
  expect(cartTotal([])).toBe(0)
})

export function cartTotal(items: number[]) {
  return items.reduce((sum, price) => sum + price)
}

## Cause found

`reduce()` needs an initial value when the array can be empty. Start the sum at **0**.

```ts
export function cartTotal(items: number[]) {
  return items.reduce((sum, price) => sum + price, 0)
}
```

This keeps non-empty totals unchanged and makes the empty cart return zero. The source has not been changed in this inspection.
